  "review_notes": "I read the whole file. I searched Mathlib for other uses of `Numbering` and for `\u2243 Fin (card ...)` types. I found no competing independent concept. `Numbering X` is an `abbrev` for `X \u2243 Fin (card X)`, so it is a named alias of the existing `Equiv` type and not a separate structure. `IsPrefix`, `prefixed` and `prefixedEquiv` are specific to the Katona method, and I found no equivalent Mathlib definition. `Fintype.card_numbering` is a theorem about a card, and the rubric excludes standalone theorem duplication. I am fairly confident there is nothing to report.",
